From fec8e8b1df74b1d796358247988e164479cbfb43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: harry <harry@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 23:21:01 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/8] bt: multi-link experiment for a second BLE device

Add CONFIG_BT_MULTI_LINK_EXPERIMENT (default n) to check whether the
SF32LB52 controller accepts a second concurrent LE link while the phone
stays connected:

- NimBLE link limit 2 when enabled
- Settings > Bluetooth keeps advertising while open, even when paired
- count slave links; legacy connection events and "connected as slave"
  follow the first (primary) link only
- double vibe when a second link connects, short vibe when it drops
- pairing is rejected on a second link so the phone bonding is kept

Also add a workflow that builds obelix with the option enabled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HAHM7gDhkyC1bGnnk4KWyY
---
 .github/workflows/build-multilink.yml   | 87 +++++++++++++++++++++++++
 pebble/apps/system/settings/bluetooth.c | 11 ++++
 pebble/comm/ble/gap_le_connect.c        | 68 +++++++++++++++++++
 pebble/comm/ble/gap_le_connect.h        |  5 ++
 pebble/popups/bluetooth_pairing_ui.c    | 12 ++++
 pebble/services/bluetooth/Kconfig       | 11 ++++
 subsys/bluetooth/Kconfig.defconfig      |  4 ++
 7 files changed, 198 insertions(+)
